# Normalize line endings to LF for everything text-based (this app deploys
# to Linux/Docker on Railway; CRLF in a shell script or Dockerfile can break
# the build). Without this, an editor/OS that writes CRLF makes every line
# of a touched file show as changed even with no real content change (see
# claude/ project doc for the 2026-09-20 session that diagnosed this across
# 61 files with zero real content difference, confirmed via
# `git diff --ignore-all-space`).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish or intentionally-CRLF files, if any turn up later, get an
# explicit override here rather than being silently renormalized.
